id: pm-lyfu7b
title: "pm assert: a bound over a measurement carrying polarity, scope, lifetime, enforcement level, and a required negative control, so every guarantee states which direction it can fail in"
description: "An assertion binds a measurement to a declared bound. Polarity is ceiling, floor, equals, zero, monotone_nondecreasing, monotone_nonincreasing, or subset_of, and exactly one is declared per assertion. Scope names the population the bound speaks for — active only, all statuses, or a filter expression — because a bound that is silently active-scoped always passes for the newest structural layer, which is how a governance improvement became indistinguishable from a relevance regression. Lifetime names what happens when the owning item reaches a terminal status: hold keeps comparing, retire stops and must record why the property stopped mattering. Enforcement level is block, warn, or observe, so a project adopts a bound by first watching it. A negative control is mandatory and must prove failure in every direction the polarity admits, which for a floor means both an undercut and a spurious pass. The owner is a typed relationship to the pm item that owns the property, not a string, so assertions participate in the graph and an item's blast radius includes the guarantees that depend on it. Tightening is automatic and monotone; loosening is refused unless a linked Decision item authorises it, which is what makes a repair and an erosion structurally different acts rather than the same hand edit."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk",assurance,configurability,enforcement,measurement-ratchet
created_at: "2026-08-10T20:55:45.036Z"
